                <pb facs="0639" n="540" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg540"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/3542: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Gibraltar</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Williams</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Gibraltar</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-10-23T13:00:00+00:00">October 23, 1936—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 23—10:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Italian ship <hi rendition="#italic">Esquilino</hi> arrived today at an early
                    hour from Naples landing 23 veterans of the Ethiopian campaign en route to
                    Tangier and Casablanca and 82 Spanish who are en route to Seville to join
                    Franco’s forces.</p>
                <p>Moorish troops continue to cross the Straits into Spain escorted by insurgent
                    warship.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Williams</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
